    "abstract": "Illustrated parts figure for the aft cargo door structure and the surround splice plates, showing the original single-row and the reinforced staggered double-row fastener arrangements as alternate items.",
    "sections": {
      "purpose": "This figure identifies the aft cargo door structural members and the longitudinal splice plates around the door cut-out, for ZEPHYR-24 aircraft in both the original and the reinforced surround standards.",
      "figure_note": "The view is taken from inside the aft cargo compartment looking outboard, with the door removed. Items 40 and 40A are the two splice plate standards and must not be mixed on one cut-out; the reinforced item is recognised by the staggered fastener pattern and by the additional outboard angle at item 60. The edging grommet at item 90 is fitted only where the wiring route crosses the fastener line, which is a customer option and is shown dashed."
    },
